{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 989,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mathematics is a powerful tool in physics,\ndescribing everything from the shapes of planetary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6049,
    "dDurationMs": 4241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbits to the properties of atoms. Math was\nused to predict the existence of the planet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10290,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neptune, radio waves and the Higgs Boson.\nSome think it means nothing profound, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15051,
    "dDurationMs": 4039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that math is simply something we've made up\nto be useful. Others think it means that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19090,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's something fundamentally mathematical\nabout nature. The most extreme possibility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23330,
    "dDurationMs": 5209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that our universe is completely mathematical,\nin the sense that it has no properties except"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28539,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematical properties. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29590,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at first glance, our universe doesn't\nseem very mathematical at all. A sheep has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34900,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "properties such as cuteness and fluffiness\n— not mathematical properties. Yet we know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39560,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this sheep - and everything else in our\nuniverse — is ultimately made of elementary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43180,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles such as electrons and quarks. And\nwhat properties does an electron have? Smell? Color?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48300,
    "dDurationMs": 8870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Texture? No, only properties like -1, ½ and\n1! We physicists call these properties electric charge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57170,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spin and lepton number, but the electron doesn't care\nwhat we call them: the fundamental properties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61890,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that an electron has are just numbers, mathematical\nproperties. As far as we know, all elementary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67190,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles, the building blocks of everything around,\nare purely mathematical objects in the sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71820,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they don't have any properties except\nfor mathematical properties. The same goes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75619,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the space that these particles are in -\nfor example, it has the property 3, the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80050,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of dimensions. If space is mathematical and\neverything in space is also mathematical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85030,
    "dDurationMs": 4729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the idea that everything is mathematical\ndoesn't sound as crazy anymore. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89759,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum mechanics and string theory introduce\neven more mathematical structures, with nerdy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93860,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "names like Hilbert space, linear operators\nand Calabi-Yau manifolds. We physicists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99220,
    "dDurationMs": 4689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still haven't found any properties of nature\nthat we can prove are non-mathematical, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103909,
    "dDurationMs": 4911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is why some of us - including me - think that\nperhaps there just isn't anything else out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108820,
    "dDurationMs": 24100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there, other than math. And that thought\nmakes me one positively awestruck "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132920,
    "dDurationMs": 16740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematical object."
    } ]
  } ]
}
